## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using the software.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Only noncommercial purposes are permitted under this license. A noncommercial purpose is one that is not directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation, directly or indirectly.

Commercial use is not permitted. This includes selling or renting the software; charging for access to it; using it for paid DJ performances, commercial venue entertainment, monetized broadcasts or streams, paid services, commercial products, or the operation of a business. Providing the software itself without charge does not make an otherwise commercial use noncommercial.

These restrictions apply to use, modification, and distribution of the software and works based on it. Commercial use requires a separate written license from the relevant copyright holder.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for the benefit of public knowledge, personal study, private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or religious observance, without any anticipated commercial application, is use for a permitted purpose.

## Organizations

Individuals and organizations may use the software for permitted noncommercial purposes. Charitable, educational, governmental, or nonprofit status does not by itself permit a commercial use.

